{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgvpskb2GS6LErjcfRa71","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015cBsrY8CPcnXZquM57FZxK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep('step (a) below without','step (a) above without')\nrep('the evaluator then re-verifies independently.','the evaluator records its own verified budget for the returned set.')\nrep('Its held-out evaluation completed and was recorded as qualified. We read this as: the evaluation ran to completion and its controls passed. It is not evidence','Its held-out evaluation completed and was recorded as qualified, with a true success indicator. The evidence does not record which gate criteria the qualification decision covers, so we read it only as a statement that the sealed evaluation ran to completion and was recorded as qualified; we do not read it as certifying controls or validity. The control outcomes in Section~\\\\ref{sec:controls} are separate observations taken from the recorded episodes. Qualification is not evidence')\nrep('\\\\subsection{Controls}\\n','\\\\subsection{Controls}\\\\label{sec:controls}\\n')\nrep('The qualified outcome of the held-out evaluation certifies that the evaluation completed with its controls passing; it neither establishes','The held-out evaluation was recorded as qualified, but the qualification criteria are not recorded in the evidence, so this outcome neither establishes')\nrep('The held-out evaluation completed with outcome qualified, and the recorded success indicator is true. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.outcome]]','The held-out evaluation completed with outcome qualified, and the recorded success indicator is true. The evidence does not record the gate criteria behind this outcome, so we do not interpret it as certifying that controls passed or that the evaluation is valid beyond the cases reported. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.outcome]]')\nrep('The cross-table copy control applied the removal set of F1 to F3 and of F3 to F1, with indices rescaled by the ratio of table sizes, and produced 0 flips in 2 trials.','The cross-table copy control recorded 0 flips in 2 trials; its construction is not documented in the staged evidence.')\nrep('both non-vacuous by the evaluator\\'s criterion.','both recorded as non-vacuous by the evaluator.')\nrep('the permutation controls were non-vacuous in the evaluator\\'s sense','the permutation controls were recorded as non-vacuous by the evaluator') if 'the permutation controls were non-vacuous' in s else None\nrep('The permutation controls were non-vacuous in the evaluator\\'s sense (Figure','The permutation controls were recorded as non-vacuous by the evaluator (Figure')\n# normaliser\nrep('Dividing by the mean number of comparisons a participant appears in ($2N/M$, derived: 5,217 for the crowd table and 860 for the sports table) instead of by $N$ reverses the direction of the size effect: the 62-row top-pair budget is 1.2\\\\% of a crowd participant\\'s comparisons and 7.2\\\\% of a team\\'s, and the mid-pair budgets are 0.077\\\\% and 0.93\\\\%.','Dividing instead by the mean number of comparisons a participant appears in ($2N/M$, derived: 5,217 for the crowd table and 860 for the sports table) shrinks the contrast but does not remove it: the 62-row top-pair budget is 1.2\\\\% of a crowd participant\\'s comparisons and 7.2\\\\% of a team\\'s (about 6 times), and the mid-pair budgets are 0.077\\\\% and 0.93\\\\% (about 12 times), against 10.5 and 21.0 times under $k/N$.')\nrep('Both views give the same qualitative picture (small budgets, mid cheaper than top), but they disagree about which table looks more fragile.','Both views give the same qualitative picture (small budgets, mid cheaper than top, sports the larger share), differing in the size of the ratio.')\n# Table dev: restrict\nrep('''Influence-guided (studied) & 0.4993 & 0.9987 & 0.0 & 0.5 & 1.3\\\\\\\\\nCell-aggregated relaxed search & 0.4993 & 0.9987 & 0.0 & 0.5 & 2.0\\\\\\\\\nStationarity linear program & 0.4993 & 0.9987 & 0.0 & 0.5 & 114\\\\\\\\''','''Configuration 1 (studied) & 0.4993 & 0.9987$^\\\\dagger$ & 0.0$^\\\\dagger$ & 0.5$^\\\\dagger$ & 1.3\\\\\\\\\nConfiguration 2 & 0.4993 & -- & -- & -- & 2.0\\\\\\\\\nConfiguration 3 & 0.4993 & -- & -- & -- & 114\\\\\\\\''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"Development evaluation (Arena\" paper.tex; sed -n 214,222p paper.tex"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1988,"cache_read_input_tokens":77569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1988},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35d0884b-633b-4c96-8540-7a451c3c9e1e","uuid":"d92427bc-27bd-4a00-b47a-3d080edf0227","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:29:24.408Z","request_id":"req_011CgvpsjntMNSek9pKx3P5t"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015cBsrY8CPcnXZquM57FZxK","type":"tool_result","content":"221:\\caption{Development evaluation (Arena 55k and MT-Bench human; seeds 11 and 12). Scores are not comparable with held-out scores, which use different tables.}\n\n\\subsection{Development tables: a three-way tie and an unflipped expert table}\\label{sec:dev}\nTable~\\ref{tab:dev} reports the development evaluation of three search configurations: the influence-guided configuration studied above, a configuration that aggregates rows into cells and solves a relaxed removal problem with exact swap polishing, and one that solves a stationarity linear program over target ratings. All three scored 0.4993, the same as the starting baseline (difference 0.0); all three were scored (3 of 3, none missing). % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study]]\nThe evaluator's own influence-only reference scored 0.4993 as well, and the random reference 0.0695. The score splits into 0.9987 on the crowd family (Arena 55k) and 0.0 on the expert family (MT-Bench human). Per-episode runtimes were about 1.3 s, 2.0 s and 114 s. We include the second and third configurations only as evidence that added search sophistication did not change the outcome; their source is not part of the staged inspectable evidence, so we make no statement about their implementation beyond the descriptions above.\n\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Development evaluation (Arena 55k and MT-Bench human; seeds 11 and 12). Scores are not comparable with held-out scores, which use different tables.}\n\\label{tab:dev}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35d0884b-633b-4c96-8540-7a451c3c9e1e","uuid":"1c28f6ec-3505-4a50-8c0f-e49be422cfca","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:29:24.480Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"221:\\caption{Development evaluation (Arena 55k and MT-Bench human; seeds 11 and 12). Scores are not comparable with held-out scores, which use different tables.}\n\n\\subsection{Development tables: a three-way tie and an unflipped expert table}\\label{sec:dev}\nTable~\\ref{tab:dev} reports the development evaluation of three search configurations: the influence-guided configuration studied above, a configuration that aggregates rows into cells and solves a relaxed removal problem with exact swap polishing, and one that solves a stationarity linear program over target ratings. All three scored 0.4993, the same as the starting baseline (difference 0.0); all three were scored (3 of 3, none missing). % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study]]\nThe evaluator's own influence-only reference scored 0.4993 as well, and the random reference 0.0695. The score splits into 0.9987 on the crowd family (Arena 55k) and 0.0 on the expert family (MT-Bench human). Per-episode runtimes were about 1.3 s, 2.0 s and 114 s. We include the second and third configurations only as evidence that added search sophistication did not change the outcome; their source is not part of the staged inspectable evidence, so we make no statement about their implementation beyond the descriptions above.\n\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Development evaluation (Arena 55k and MT-Bench human; seeds 11 and 12). Scores are not comparable with held-out scores, which use different tables.}\n\\label{tab:dev}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
