{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvptjjCE9Vji642RY89U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017QgPMAqLZH4VvDxSevXVKv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np='paper.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep('Table~\\\\ref{tab:dev} reports the development evaluation of three search configurations: the influence-guided configuration studied above, a configuration that aggregates rows into cells and solves a relaxed removal problem with exact swap polishing, and one that solves a stationarity linear program over target ratings. All three scored','Table~\\\\ref{tab:dev} reports the development evaluation of three search configurations: the influence-guided configuration studied above (Configuration 1) and two further configurations that are identified in the evidence only by their titles, a cell-aggregated relaxed removal search (Configuration 2) and a stationarity-LP target-rating search (Configuration 3). All three scored')\nrep('''The evaluator's own influence-only reference scored 0.4993 as well, and the random reference 0.0695. The score splits into 0.9987 on the crowd family (Arena 55k) and 0.0 on the expert family (MT-Bench human). Per-episode runtimes were about 1.3 s, 2.0 s and 114 s. We include the second and third configurations only as evidence that added search sophistication did not change the outcome; their source is not part of the staged inspectable evidence, so we make no statement about their implementation beyond the descriptions above.''','''For the studied configuration, the search-stage evaluator output splits this score into 0.9987 on the crowd family (Arena 55k) and 0.0 on the expert family (MT-Bench human), with an influence-only reference of 0.4993 and a random reference of 0.0695. These sub-scores are quoted from that logged evaluator output and have no entry in the evidence registry, which records only the three total scores and per-episode runtimes (about 1.3 s, 2.0 s and 114 s). We therefore give no breakdown for Configurations 2 and 3. Their source is not part of the staged inspectable evidence, so we make no statement about their algorithms beyond their titles; we mention them only because their total score did not exceed that of the starting baseline.''')\nrep('Scores are not comparable with held-out scores, which use different tables.}','Scores are not comparable with held-out scores, which use different tables. $^\\\\dagger$Quoted from the logged search-stage evaluator output; no registry entry. Dashes: no grounded breakdown.}')\nrep('Besides the scores in Table~\\\\ref{tab:dev}, the development evaluation reported a random-removal reference of 0.0695, an influence-only reference of 0.4993, a mean budget fraction (of the cap, averaged over the four non-control cases) of 0.5007, and a permuted-minus-real control gap of 0.3153. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#all_programs]]','Besides the scores in Table~\\\\ref{tab:dev}, the logged search-stage evaluator output for the studied configuration reports a random-removal reference of 0.0695, an influence-only reference of 0.4993, a mean budget fraction (of the cap, averaged over the four non-control cases) of 0.5007, and a permuted-minus-real control gap of 0.3153. These figures are quoted from that log and are not entries of the evidence registry. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#all_programs]] total score only')\nrep('the influence-guided configuration studied above, ','the influence-guided configuration studied above, ') if False else None\n# data provenance SI\nrep('The held-out tables are prepared by the evaluator and are checked by checksum; their content hashes are tested for overlap with development data and the evaluation aborts on any overlap.','The held-out tables are prepared by the evaluator; the evaluator metadata records the content-overlap removals and prompt-only overlaps reported in Section~4.1, and we have no further documentation of its preparation or checking procedure.')\n# SI algorithmic spec\nrep('The evaluator\\'s fit and the candidate\\'s fit use the same objective; the evaluator\\'s acceptance test is $\\\\theta_{\\\\hi}<\\\\theta_{\\\\lo}$ with no margin. ','The candidate\\'s own acceptance test uses a margin of $10^{-5}$ on its own fit; how the evaluator\\'s fit and acceptance test are implemented is not documented in the staged evidence. ')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"Section~4.1\" paper.tex | head -2; grep -n \"Experimental Protocol\\|\\\\\\\\subsection{Data}\" paper.tex|head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2595,"cache_read_input_tokens":79557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2595},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35d0884b-633b-4c96-8540-7a451c3c9e1e","uuid":"83a4d8dd-3bfc-4661-83ec-cf0350b93d59","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:29:37.420Z","request_id":"req_011Cgvptiuqu5rtjCDT6Pipm"}
