{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHcZtJGr7pNKLYZrp3ZHmK","type":"tool_result","content":"132:\\caption{Protocol overview. An anonymised comparison table is fit with a ridge-penalised Bradley--Terry model; a target adjacent pair (top or mid) is selected; a removal search proposes at most $2\\%$ of rows; the evaluator refits exactly and records the verified budget $k$ and score $1-k/\\kcap$. Random, influence-only and opponent-targeted removal serve as comparators; empty-set, label-permutation and cross-table copy runs serve as controls. Development tables (Arena 55k, MT-Bench human) and held-out tables (Arena 140k deduplicated, NBA) are kept separate.}\n206:This is the expected direction if real budgets reflect real rating gaps: with outcomes shuffled the ratings collapse together and a handful of rows reorders them. It does not show that real ranks are robust in any absolute sense, and the permuted tables are a lower reference, not a model of noise or manipulation.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35d0884b-633b-4c96-8540-7a451c3c9e1e","uuid":"4d455fb8-6ed5-415f-9d70-a72719998558","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:29:43.771Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"132:\\caption{Protocol overview. An anonymised comparison table is fit with a ridge-penalised Bradley--Terry model; a target adjacent pair (top or mid) is selected; a removal search proposes at most $2\\%$ of rows; the evaluator refits exactly and records the verified budget $k$ and score $1-k/\\kcap$. Random, influence-only and opponent-targeted removal serve as comparators; empty-set, label-permutation and cross-table copy runs serve as controls. Development tables (Arena 55k, MT-Bench human) and held-out tables (Arena 140k deduplicated, NBA) are kept separate.}\n206:This is the expected direction if real budgets reflect real rating gaps: with outcomes shuffled the ratings collapse together and a handful of rows reorders them. It does not show that real ranks are robust in any absolute sense, and the permuted tables are a lower reference, not a model of noise or manipulation.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
