--- final message ---
I fixed the figure-manifest error and all four audit findings. The paper compiles, with the body ending on page 9. The evidence verifier reports 0 dangling references, and `validate_tex_refs.py` passes. I couldn't run the orchestrator's own checks here: `validate_figures.py` needs a `src` package that isn't in this workspace, and `compile_latex.sh` needs `pdftotext`, which is missing. So the manifest fix is untested against the real validator, and the 75% page-fill check hasn't been run.

**Figure manifest**
- `controls_permutation` had `figure_type: paired_panel_bar`, which the schema rejects. I changed it to `bar`.
- That one bad entry also produced the "missing required figure" errors for all three figures.
- I set the controls figure to 0.75 of the text width, in both the TeX and the manifest. This shortened the page enough to keep the body within 9 pages.

**Audit findings**
- **Normaliser direction:** the paper no longer says the direction reverses or that the views disagree. It now says the sports table has the larger budget share under both normalisers: about 6× (top) and 12× (mid) per participant, against 10.5× and 21.0× per table row. The confound caveat is kept.
- **"Qualified" over-read:** the paper now says only that the held-out evaluation completed, was recorded as qualified, and has a true success indicator. It states that the qualification criteria are not recorded, so it does not read qualified as certifying controls or validity. The empty-set, permutation and copy results are reported as separate observations, and I added a pointer from the qualification text to them.
- **Evaluator internals:** I removed the comparator and control details I couldn't verify from staged evidence:
  - how the three comparators are built;
  - the permutation thresholds;
  - the no-margin acceptance rule;
  - the abort-on-overlap and checksum behaviour;
  - the copy-control rescaling;
  - the row bit-width and chunking.

  The paper now reports only recorded outcomes, and says my reading of the influence-only comparator is an interpretation, not a verified fact.
- **Development breakdown:** the development table now gives only the total score and runtime for configurations 2 and 3, and describes them by title only. The studied configuration's sub-scores are flagged as quoted from the logged search-stage output, with no registry entry. I updated claims 12, 17 and 19 in `claims_grounding.json` to match and added one claim about the unverified evaluator internals. All 29 claims have source IDs that resolve.

**Other changes**
- A reference title in `references.bib` contained a garbled character that broke compilation, so I rewrote it as `$\ell_\infty$`.
- I trimmed prose in the introduction, related work, discussion and conclusion to get the body back to 9 pages. No numbers were changed.
- One side effect of the trimming: I dropped the "prefix bisection assumes monotone flipping" sentence from the threats paragraph. It is still stated in the method section.

I appended the repair entries to `memory.md`, `global_memory/memory.md` and `global_memory/memory.jsonl`.
